<Layout title="How to Play — Large Print Crosswords" active="help"><div class="container prose"><header class="page-heading"><p class="eyebrow">A HELPING HAND</p><h1>A few simple steps.</h1><p>You do not need to be an expert. A little curiosity is all it takes.</p></header><h2>Start with a clue</h2><p>Choose a clue under Across or Down. Its squares will turn pale green, and your current square will turn gold. Type the answer one letter at a time. The number in parentheses tells you how many letters to use.</p><h2>Move around the puzzle</h2><p>Use the arrow keys to move, or tap a square. At a crossing, tap the square again or press Enter to switch between Across and Down. Backspace erases a letter. Tab takes you out of the board and on to the buttons.</p><p>These are themed mini crosswords with open layouts. Some letters are shared by two words; other letters belong to just one word. The puzzles use American English and everyday definitions.</p><h2>Choose your keyboard</h2><p>On a phone or small tablet, tapping a square opens our on-screen keyboard. It shows only letters, plus <strong>Delete</strong> and <strong>Next word</strong>, with the current clue and your entered letters above the keys. Tap <strong>Use system keyboard</strong> to use your device’s keyboard instead. Your choice is remembered in this browser when storage is available.</p><p>On a computer, use your physical keyboard as usual, or choose <strong>Use on-screen keyboard</strong>. Hide the panel whenever you like; selecting a square opens it again in on-screen mode. Within the letter keys, arrow keys move between buttons and Enter enters a letter. Escape hides the panel. Browser and device support for hiding the system keyboard can vary.</p><h2>Take a hint whenever you like</h2><p><strong>Check word</strong> checks only the selected word. Incorrect letters are underlined as well as colored. <strong>Reveal letter</strong> fills one square for you. There are no penalties and no timer.</p><h2>Make yourself comfortable</h2><p>Choose <strong>Larger clues</strong> to enlarge the clue text. You can also use your browser’s zoom controls. Sound starts off; turn it on if you enjoy a quiet tap when you enter a letter. Your sound and clue-size choices are remembered in this browser when storage is available.</p><h2>Leave and come back</h2><p>Your letters are saved automatically in this browser on this device. Private browsing, clearing browser data, or changing devices can remove or separate your progress. No account is needed.</p><h2>Print a paper copy</h2><p>Open any puzzle and select <strong>Print this puzzle</strong>. On the print page, select <strong>Print puzzle</strong>. Choose US Letter paper in portrait orientation and turn off browser headers and footers. The answers have their own page, so there are no accidental spoilers.</p><p>To download a PDF, choose <strong>Save as PDF</strong> instead of a printer in your browser’s print window. You may print puzzles for personal use and noncommercial group activities.</p><a class="button" href="/daily/">Try a puzzle →</a></div></Layout>
